From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vipul Cariappa <vipulcariappa@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:17:47 +0530
Subject: Look symbols up by IR name when the linker name misses

getAddressOfGlobal resolved a symbol by its linker name only, carrying a
`// TODO: Or getSymbolAddress` on the line. Which of the two spellings works
depends on the executor, and the wasm one resolves symbols with dlsym, where
only IR names exist -- so every linker-name lookup missed everything the JIT
had produced.

compileFunction is what makes that fatal. It parses the wrapper, then asks
getAddressOfGlobal for it, and returns null if the lookup comes up empty -- with
no diagnostic, because nothing failed to compile. JitCall then reports
"TClingCallFunc::make_wrapper:Failed to compile" and dumps source that is
perfectly valid; feeding that same text to Declare and looking the symbol up by
IR name hands back an address. The effect was that MakeFunctionCallable failed
for *every* function under wasm, `int add(int, int)` included, so nothing built
on JitCall could call anything.

Try the linker name first, exactly as before, and fall back to the IR name
before giving up. Where the linker name already resolves, the fallback never
runs.

(cherry picked from commit 1f16f33a2c7a87acb187724d82106e732fa1e021)
---
 lib/CppInterOp/CppInterOpInterpreter.h | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/CppInterOp/CppInterOpInterpreter.h b/lib/CppInterOp/CppInterOpInterpreter.h
index cd3a9ba..ede6339 100644
--- a/lib/CppInterOp/CppInterOpInterpreter.h
+++ b/lib/CppInterOp/CppInterOpInterpreter.h
@@ -433,12 +433,22 @@ public:
     if (isInSyntaxOnlyMode())
       return nullptr;
 
-    auto addressOrErr =
-        getSymbolAddressFromLinkerName(SymName); // TODO: Or getSymbolAddress
+    auto addressOrErr = getSymbolAddressFromLinkerName(SymName);
     if (addressOrErr)
       return addressOrErr->toPtr<void*>();
-
-    llvm::consumeError(addressOrErr.takeError()); // okay to be missing
+    llvm::consumeError(addressOrErr.takeError());
+
+    // Fall back to the IR name. Which of the two spellings resolves depends on
+    // the executor: the wasm one looks symbols up with dlsym and only ever sees
+    // IR names, so a linker-name lookup misses everything the JIT produced.
+    // compileFunction leans on this to hand back the wrapper it just built, and
+    // a miss there is silent -- it reports the compile as failed, for code that
+    // compiled cleanly.
+    auto irOrErr = getSymbolAddress(SymName);
+    if (irOrErr)
+      return irOrErr->toPtr<void*>();
+
+    llvm::consumeError(irOrErr.takeError()); // okay to be missing
     return nullptr;
   }
 
